{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520539811,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMDM2MTUwMDA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2290","origin":"github"},"title":"More specifically specify relationship between datasets were possible","message":"#### What is the problem?\nATM with #2289 we would get basic (partOf) relationship between subdatasets.\n [FAIR I3](https://www.go-fair.org/fair-principles/i3-metadata-include-qualified-references-metadata/) desires to have \"more qualified\" relationships declared.  In our datasets most typical and often presented relationship is having a derivative dataset:\n- `./derivatives/subds1` isDerivativeOf  '.' but it goes backward in the hierarchy since we are aggregating into the superdataset.  So I may be we could have `hasDerivatives` similar to `hasParts`?\n- in case of hierarchies where original dataset is subdataset (like @mih does in study forrest) then isDerivativeOf would work natively\n\nAny other relationship we could have?","files":null}]}